(1871617, 254797, 42277, '<td valign="top">I hear everyone on the noise.  It was a little overdone after viewing it again.  As for the pole, it annoyed the hell out of me.  Unfortunately, it was pouring down rain so I couldn''t step out further to frame it out, and cropping it lost a lot of the interesting wall at the right edge of the frame.  Thanks for the feedback</td>', 'I hear everyone on the noise.  It was a little overdone after viewing it again.  As for the pole, it annoyed the hell out of me.  Unfortunately, it was pouring down rain so I couldn''t step out further to frame it out, and cropping it lost a lot of the interesting wall at the right edge of the frame.  Thanks for the feedback', '2005-11-16 02:50:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1871659, 254819, 21604, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Gary Murakami:</b></div><hr/><i> Is that ice?  Made me look longer than expected, and suspected construction is more respected for the ice. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>yup it is ice - don''t think many others "got" the idea tho!</td>', 'Originally posted by Gary Murakami: Is that ice?  Made me look longer than expected, and suspected construction is more respected for the ice.   yup it is ice - don''t think many others "got" the idea tho!', '2005-11-16 03:05:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1871695, 254617, 47390, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all good critics, glad you enjoyed it.<br/>Lots of people think that I have used selective saturation or adjusted channels, but this is how it looks in reality, although auto contrast showed the true colors as the shot was taken a very clody day and the original histogram showed only app. 2-3 stops.<br/> <br/>This is my first entry in DP-challenge so a 4th place is really nice (a ribbon would of course been a better start, =) I would just have neededa 0.007 more...<br/> <br/>Tried a lot off differnet crops, but without the water reflection it just lost a lot.<br/> <br/>Thanks everyone.</td>', 'Thanks for all good critics, glad you enjoyed it.Lots of people think that I have used selective saturation or adjusted channels, but this is how it looks in reality, although auto contrast showed the true colors as the shot was taken a very clody day and the original histogram showed only app. 2-3 stops. This is my first entry in DP-challenge so a 4th place is really nice (a ribbon would of course been a better start, =) I would just have neededa 0.007 more... Tried a lot off differnet crops, but without the water reflection it just lost a lot. Thanks everyone.', '2005-11-16 03:27:51.000000', NULL, 0),
