(1873725, 255270, 46870, '<td valign="top">wow '' funny and perfect pic. Congratulations</td>', 'wow '' funny and perfect pic. Congratulations', '2005-11-16 15:01:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1873728, 254164, 40718, '<td valign="top">I think it is more unconventional and harder to pull off when the foreground is out of the DOF and the background is within the DOF.  The foreground commands so much more of the space and people are disconcerted when it is OOF.<br/> <br/>The lighting and other technicals seem great.  I don''t think there is a cast and there appears to be ample contrast.  The composition is nice, although perhaps a little too symmetrical.<br/> <br/>You got a few 1-votes from the pro-smoking crowd no doubt.</td>', 'I think it is more unconventional and harder to pull off when the foreground is out of the DOF and the background is within the DOF.  The foreground commands so much more of the space and people are disconcerted when it is OOF. The lighting and other technicals seem great.  I don''t think there is a cast and there appears to be ample contrast.  The composition is nice, although perhaps a little too symmetrical. You got a few 1-votes from the pro-smoking crowd no doubt.', '2005-11-16 15:01:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1873742, 255265, 40718, '<td valign="top">I like the composition, although I think we want to see a little more of her? face.  It''s sorta nice she''s shutting us out a bit, but we want to see the emotion.  I have a hunch this is staged as her clothes look pretty clean and new. :)<br/> <br/>I think the sepia isn''t doing you any favors.  B&amp;W would have been better.  I always ask what purpose I''m trying to accomplish when I add an effect.  If it''s just to "look cool", I usually wind up going with simpler.  It almost always works better.<br/> <br/>The lighting is a bit harsh too.  Looks like a utility light which casts harsh dark shadows.  I think dark shadows would be good in this pic, but they aren''t utilized at all.  Side lighting might be more dramatic here.</td>', 'I like the composition, although I think we want to see a little more of her? face.  It''s sorta nice she''s shutting us out a bit, but we want to see the emotion.  I have a hunch this is staged as her clothes look pretty clean and new. :) I think the sepia isn''t doing you any favors.  B&W would have been better.  I always ask what purpose I''m trying to accomplish when I add an effect.  If it''s just to "look cool", I usually wind up going with simpler.  It almost always works better. The lighting is a bit harsh too.  Looks like a utility light which casts harsh dark shadows.  I think dark shadows would be good in this pic, but they aren''t utilized at all.  Side lighting might be more dramatic here.', '2005-11-16 15:05:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1873751, 255474, 40718, '<td valign="top">It just looks too nice for garbage.  The lighting is wonderful.  I need to make my own lightbox someday too.  But it all looks too staged and antiseptic.  I think that''s your biggest problem.  The composition isn''t bad, but is too symmetrical and centered.  We have 4 elements all mirroring each other.  That adds to the unrealistic nature.  I think we wanted our garbage to look like garbage...(see ribbon winners).</td>', 'It just looks too nice for garbage.  The lighting is wonderful.  I need to make my own lightbox someday too.  But it all looks too staged and antiseptic.  I think that''s your biggest problem.  The composition isn''t bad, but is too symmetrical and centered.  We have 4 elements all mirroring each other.  That adds to the unrealistic nature.  I think we wanted our garbage to look like garbage...(see ribbon winners).', '2005-11-16 15:08:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1873770, 253601, 40718, '<td valign="top">Since the colors don''t do much for this picture, I would think B&amp;W to go for the texture.  You have nice textures in the rubble and the rebar makes a nice pattern against the sky.  The bush also hurts your image because it''s a muddy green/black chunk of no detail.  Dark green like evergreens is really hard to photograph well.  I would have recomposed to remove the bush.  I''m guessing you took this on the fly because of the truck so you probably didn''t have time to think about this stuff.<br/> <br/>Focus and DOF is nice.  So much sky in the picture is never really good blown out.  Either expose for the sky (and see if you can get away with it on the ground objects), or recompose so the sky isn''t as dominant.</td>', 'Since the colors don''t do much for this picture, I would think B&W to go for the texture.  You have nice textures in the rubble and the rebar makes a nice pattern against the sky.  The bush also hurts your image because it''s a muddy green/black chunk of no detail.  Dark green like evergreens is really hard to photograph well.  I would have recomposed to remove the bush.  I''m guessing you took this on the fly because of the truck so you probably didn''t have time to think about this stuff. Focus and DOF is nice.  So much sky in the picture is never really good blown out.  Either expose for the sky (and see if you can get away with it on the ground objects), or recompose so the sky isn''t as dominant.', '2005-11-16 15:16:26.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(1873779, 252555, 40718, '<td valign="top">The coversion to B&amp;W is excellent.  Very well done.  The composition could maybe be a bit stronger with a little less centeredness.  Perhaps shift to the left toward the sign.  The sign is better than the big pole in the background.<br/> <br/>Ultimately the subject probably got you.  It''s too "snapshot" or mundane.  We see fat guys throw away trash every day.  Why are we looking at a picture of it?  That being said, you did as well as you could. I''d have given a 6 just for the crisp B&amp;W.</td>', 'The coversion to B&W is excellent.  Very well done.  The composition could maybe be a bit stronger with a little less centeredness.  Perhaps shift to the left toward the sign.  The sign is better than the big pole in the background. Ultimately the subject probably got you.  It''s too "snapshot" or mundane.  We see fat guys throw away trash every day.  Why are we looking at a picture of it?  That being said, you did as well as you could. I''d have given a 6 just for the crisp B&W.', '2005-11-16 15:19:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1873793, 255598, 714, '<td valign="top">Very creative image!  You rock no matter what place you take!</td>', 'Very creative image!  You rock no matter what place you take!', '2005-11-16 15:21:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1873901, 255592, 21714, '<td valign="top">This was my favourite in the challenge. <br/>Forget the challenge - it''s a geat image. I know I will always enjoy this one.</td>', 'This was my favourite in the challenge. Forget the challenge - it''s a geat image. I know I will always enjoy this one.', '2005-11-16 15:51:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1873968, 255265, 8455, '<td valign="top">I remember thinking about this one during the challenge.  It''s a great emotive shot, and I personally like the fact that she''s ''shutting us out'', to me, the situation is one of aloneness and hardship.  One thing that somewhat put me off is that since the title of the challenge is ''garbage'' and the main focus of the image is a homeless person, it could be interpreted as a statement about the ''waste/garbage of society''... though I don''t think (I hope and your title indicates) that was the intent.  Nevertheless, the implication bothered me.<br/> <br/>On a photographic note, I do think the lighting was a bit intense, as the shadow right behind her is the only really stark/black part of the image.</td>', 'I remember thinking about this one during the challenge.  It''s a great emotive shot, and I personally like the fact that she''s ''shutting us out'', to me, the situation is one of aloneness and hardship.  One thing that somewhat put me off is that since the title of the challenge is ''garbage'' and the main focus of the image is a homeless person, it could be interpreted as a statement about the ''waste/garbage of society''... though I don''t think (I hope and your title indicates) that was the intent.  Nevertheless, the implication bothered me. On a photographic note, I do think the lighting was a bit intense, as the shadow right behind her is the only really stark/black part of the image.', '2005-11-16 16:12:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(1873992, 253314, 11738, '<td valign="top">Sorry that you lost your for a dates violation.  Don''t let it discourage.  Please keep submitting and sharing with the community.</td>', 'Sorry that you lost your for a dates violation.  Don''t let it discourage.  Please keep submitting and sharing with the community.', '2005-11-16 16:19:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874031, 254617, 3214, '<td valign="top">OK, I''m just happy now that you got a ribbon for this superb shot.</td>', 'OK, I''m just happy now that you got a ribbon for this superb shot.', '2005-11-16 16:30:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874043, 255590, 3214, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your brown ribbon!  ;-)</td>', 'Congrats on your brown ribbon!  ;-)', '2005-11-16 16:32:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874060, 254468, 3214, '<td valign="top">Well, it''s only peripherally garbage from a photography standpoint (one crumpled piece of paper), conceptually I enjoyed your depiction of coverups as garbage a.k.a. crap and scored higher accordingly.</td>', 'Well, it''s only peripherally garbage from a photography standpoint (one crumpled piece of paper), conceptually I enjoyed your depiction of coverups as garbage a.k.a. crap and scored higher accordingly.', '2005-11-16 16:36:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874089, 254468, 12253, '<td valign="top">I thought this was hillarious!  Great job regardless of your placement here (political messages sometime have drawbacks).  (I was one of your 9''s)</td>', 'I thought this was hillarious!  Great job regardless of your placement here (political messages sometime have drawbacks).  (I was one of your 9''s)', '2005-11-16 16:45:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874139, 254108, 40718, '<td valign="top">I sorta like this one.  I''m not sure about the blue tint though.  Rebar makes me think of rusty red.  Either going with the natural tint or trying B&amp;W since this is a picture mainly concerned with shapes and patterns (color isn''t an issue with those so why use it?).<br/> <br/>The white splotch is too bad and you probably could have done something about it.  A bit overexposed on the middle highlight.  The composition is nice though.</td>', 'I sorta like this one.  I''m not sure about the blue tint though.  Rebar makes me think of rusty red.  Either going with the natural tint or trying B&W since this is a picture mainly concerned with shapes and patterns (color isn''t an issue with those so why use it?). The white splotch is too bad and you probably could have done something about it.  A bit overexposed on the middle highlight.  The composition is nice though.', '2005-11-16 17:03:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874146, 253017, 40718, '<td valign="top">An interesting idea.  I think I would have pulled that weed? that is over the cup.  It isn''t obvious what it is so distracts people from the subject.  As weird as this sounds, you could have picked better trash. White styrafoam is hard to make look good (maybe a non-white paper cup) as is a baggie (a chip bag instead?).<br/> <br/>I would have removed the other weed that is entering from the left.  Controlling the whole canvas is always important.  If it isn''t adding something, get rid of it.<br/> <br/>Your conversion to B&amp;W isn''t too bad.  A little harsh on the RR track highlight.</td>', 'An interesting idea.  I think I would have pulled that weed? that is over the cup.  It isn''t obvious what it is so distracts people from the subject.  As weird as this sounds, you could have picked better trash. White styrafoam is hard to make look good (maybe a non-white paper cup) as is a baggie (a chip bag instead?). I would have removed the other weed that is entering from the left.  Controlling the whole canvas is always important.  If it isn''t adding something, get rid of it. Your conversion to B&W isn''t too bad.  A little harsh on the RR track highlight.', '2005-11-16 17:06:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874163, 255422, 40718, '<td valign="top">Dark things with detail, I find, are very hard to photograph properly.  The whole left third of your picture qualifies.  The bushes look like a murky mess.<br/> <br/>The composition isn''t bad.  I like the trash cans, which are the main subject in this challenge, are far to one side which is interesting.<br/> <br/>A number of other pictures I commented on had the same issue with color.  The colors here are unimportant and unimpressive, so try B&amp;W.  The picture then becomes more about texture and pattern and the detail of the detrius on the ground becomes more interesting.</td>', 'Dark things with detail, I find, are very hard to photograph properly.  The whole left third of your picture qualifies.  The bushes look like a murky mess. The composition isn''t bad.  I like the trash cans, which are the main subject in this challenge, are far to one side which is interesting. A number of other pictures I commented on had the same issue with color.  The colors here are unimportant and unimpressive, so try B&W.  The picture then becomes more about texture and pattern and the detail of the detrius on the ground becomes more interesting.', '2005-11-16 17:10:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874168, 255447, 28029, '<td valign="top">Very nice composition. Congratulations on your top 10 finish! Keep up the good work.<br/>               --JR</td>', 'Very nice composition. Congratulations on your top 10 finish! Keep up the good work.               --JR', '2005-11-16 17:12:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874374, 255465, 31637, '<td valign="top">This is fantastic. A rare image and well captured. Congrats !</td>', 'This is fantastic. A rare image and well captured. Congrats !', '2005-11-16 18:07:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874403, 255537, 31637, '<td valign="top">great street shot! Nice placing , your on a roll !</td>', 'great street shot! Nice placing , your on a roll !', '2005-11-16 18:16:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874429, 255453, 9111, '<td valign="top">wooohooo  11th place!   shoulda been higher!!<br/>:hug</td>', 'wooohooo  11th place!   shoulda been higher!!:hug', '2005-11-16 18:22:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874584, 255447, 39664, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by scamp:</b></div><hr/><i> Some people probably consider this garbage, but I think they''re great antiques! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I don''t see garbage.....I see a photo op!  I love this sort of stuff!  Beautiful junque!</td>', 'Originally posted by scamp: Some people probably consider this garbage, but I think they''re great antiques!   I don''t see garbage.....I see a photo op!  I love this sort of stuff!  Beautiful junque!', '2005-11-16 19:03:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874688, 254904, 40718, '<td valign="top">Boy, I''m not sure why you have 10 1-scores either.  I''m viewing it at 1200x800 and it does look jaggy on the needle.  At 1920x1200 it''s still jaggy on the needle.  The lighting on the needle also looks funny, like there''s a lot of artifact from saturating the yellow and red.<br/> <br/>As far as the composition and idea.  I like them a lot.  it''s creative and artistic and I would have thought the idea a winner going in.</td>', 'Boy, I''m not sure why you have 10 1-scores either.  I''m viewing it at 1200x800 and it does look jaggy on the needle.  At 1920x1200 it''s still jaggy on the needle.  The lighting on the needle also looks funny, like there''s a lot of artifact from saturating the yellow and red. As far as the composition and idea.  I like them a lot.  it''s creative and artistic and I would have thought the idea a winner going in.', '2005-11-16 19:29:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874690, 255453, 39664, '<td valign="top">WTG Laurie!  Well deserved and wonderful shot! ~C</td>', 'WTG Laurie!  Well deserved and wonderful shot! ~C', '2005-11-16 19:30:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874943, 255603, 12253, '<td valign="top">Rose, I had trouble seeing it too.  The problem is that you can''t see the depth of the box spring; it almost looks like a blanket has been spread out.  It would never cross my mind that the bumps were springs--a blanket on the ground also has bumps from whatever it''s on.  I think the moral of the story is that, generally, the focal point of the shot should be what cues you to the challenge topic.  I''ve learned that lesson here a time or two myself!</td>', 'Rose, I had trouble seeing it too.  The problem is that you can''t see the depth of the box spring; it almost looks like a blanket has been spread out.  It would never cross my mind that the bumps were springs--a blanket on the ground also has bumps from whatever it''s on.  I think the moral of the story is that, generally, the focal point of the shot should be what cues you to the challenge topic.  I''ve learned that lesson here a time or two myself!', '2005-11-16 20:43:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1874978, 255447, 43714, '<td valign="top">I only considered this to be garbage because it was dumped there so carelessly to rot away. I also collect and have a great deal of these treasures in my home!</td>', 'I only considered this to be garbage because it was dumped there so carelessly to rot away. I also collect and have a great deal of these treasures in my home!', '2005-11-16 20:52:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1875018, 253314, 36832, '<td valign="top">Sorry about the DQ, but I still think this is a great pic!</td>', 'Sorry about the DQ, but I still think this is a great pic!', '2005-11-16 21:03:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1875161, 254617, 28532, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot!! This was one of my favorites.  Congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'Wonderful shot!! This was one of my favorites.  Congrats on the ribbon.', '2005-11-16 21:35:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1875184, 255465, 13719, '<td valign="top">wow congrats on the your first FIRST place ribbon, way to go thats awesome</td>', 'wow congrats on the your first FIRST place ribbon, way to go thats awesome', '2005-11-16 21:40:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1875350, 254617, 27763, '<td valign="top">I''m glad to see this shot ribbon.  It must be one of the most beautiful pictures of trash I''ve ever seen :)</td>', 'I''m glad to see this shot ribbon.  It must be one of the most beautiful pictures of trash I''ve ever seen :)', '2005-11-16 22:14:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1875369, 254108, 28471, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrAchoo:</b></div><hr/><i> I sorta like this one.  I''m not sure about the blue tint though.  Rebar makes me think of rusty red.  Either going with the natural tint or trying B&amp;W since this is a picture mainly concerned with shapes and patterns (color isn''t an issue with those so why use it?).<br/> <br/>The white splotch is too bad and you probably could have done something about it.  A bit overexposed on the middle highlight.  The composition is nice though. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the review.</td>', 'Originally posted by DrAchoo: I sorta like this one.  I''m not sure about the blue tint though.  Rebar makes me think of rusty red.  Either going with the natural tint or trying B&W since this is a picture mainly concerned with shapes and patterns (color isn''t an issue with those so why use it?). The white splotch is too bad and you probably could have done something about it.  A bit overexposed on the middle highlight.  The composition is nice though.   Thanks for the review.', '2005-11-16 22:16:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1875541, 255422, 42845, '<td valign="top">I really thank you very much for commenting, but I, with respect, disagree.  The lighting was intentional -- including the murkiness.  I felt the bushes were an unimportant point of interest and only needed a suggestion of detail.  As for the color, I think it defines the individual shapes of the building, the shed, the fence, and the bins.</td>', 'I really thank you very much for commenting, but I, with respect, disagree.  The lighting was intentional -- including the murkiness.  I felt the bushes were an unimportant point of interest and only needed a suggestion of detail.  As for the color, I think it defines the individual shapes of the building, the shed, the fence, and the bins.', '2005-11-16 23:11:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1875627, 254875, 42826, '<td valign="top">I think, because of the dog, you know what kind of ears it has.  So that isn''t it.  I think it''s slightly blurry, but I like the depth of field.  Voters are just very inconsistant from challenge to challenge.</td>', 'I think, because of the dog, you know what kind of ears it has.  So that isn''t it.  I think it''s slightly blurry, but I like the depth of field.  Voters are just very inconsistant from challenge to challenge.', '2005-11-16 23:32:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(1875706, 254016, 42845, '<td valign="top">I think it''s hilarious.  The lighting looks to me to be from a flashlight, as if someone heard a noise in the middle of the night and came to inspect.  With that in mind, I don''t mind the blow out highlights but instead think they add to the picture.  Anyway, the bear, after all, is perfectly exposed.</td>', 'I think it''s hilarious.  The lighting looks to me to be from a flashlight, as if someone heard a noise in the middle of the night and came to inspect.  With that in mind, I don''t mind the blow out highlights but instead think they add to the picture.  Anyway, the bear, after all, is perfectly exposed.', '2005-11-16 23:52:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1875739, 255603, 47117, '<td valign="top">nshapiro, thank you for the comment. I do understand the angle could have been better. This is why I had so many I know look at it before I entered it, and without saying anything but that I was entering it in a garbage theme, they got it and loved the idea. So many got it while voting too, so it is a bit odd to me that these questions would occur on that basis alone.  But, I think you da bomb!!  And thanks for stopping by to comment after the contest was over.  You know I am not one for comments at all on photos if you have read my comments about that elsewhere :)  But gosh, I wish those that were bagged didn''t ask questions I couldn''t answer!  See you again soon, I''m sure!!</td>', 'nshapiro, thank you for the comment. I do understand the angle could have been better. This is why I had so many I know look at it before I entered it, and without saying anything but that I was entering it in a garbage theme, they got it and loved the idea. So many got it while voting too, so it is a bit odd to me that these questions would occur on that basis alone.  But, I think you da bomb!!  And thanks for stopping by to comment after the contest was over.  You know I am not one for comments at all on photos if you have read my comments about that elsewhere :)  But gosh, I wish those that were bagged didn''t ask questions I couldn''t answer!  See you again soon, I''m sure!!', '2005-11-17 00:02:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1876097, 254617, 47390, '<td valign="top">Thanks again. Looks like a DQ made me do the cut. (though i was 0.007 points away from the ribbon anyway)</td>', 'Thanks again. Looks like a DQ made me do the cut. (though i was 0.007 points away from the ribbon anyway)', '2005-11-17 03:24:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1876109, 253314, 47390, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the ribbon. To bad you got DQed for a wrong set date. I gave you an 8. (no 10s and only one 9) so go at it again.</td>', 'Thanks for the ribbon. To bad you got DQed for a wrong set date. I gave you an 8. (no 10s and only one 9) so go at it again.', '2005-11-17 03:28:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(1876249, 255465, 36060, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the blue. A very creative picture!</td>', 'Congrats on the blue. A very creative picture!', '2005-11-17 06:04:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(1876253, 254617, 36060, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your ribbon. Great shot!</td>', 'Congrats on your ribbon. Great shot!', '2005-11-17 06:06:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1876328, 254010, 32117, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Sonifo:</b></div><hr/><i> Coming from a place like this..I find it insulting not only as a former homeless person but as a women.  You have no idea what this woman is going through or any woman in her situation at that.  You need to step down from your pedestal and into her shoes.  If she is garabe to you then you are garabe to me for thinking that. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>No hard feeelings please!<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Sonifo: Coming from a place like this..I find it insulting not only as a former homeless person but as a women.  You have no idea what this woman is going through or any woman in her situation at that.  You need to step down from your pedestal and into her shoes.  If she is garabe to you then you are garabe to me for thinking that.  No hard feeelings please!', '2005-11-17 07:10:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1876543, 254565, 19670, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by esulbi:</b></div><hr/><i> Actually, that is a softball in a pond under a bridge.  It looked all soaked and pathetic sitting there with the leaves that washed up with it.  For some reason, when I resized the photo, it lost the detail of the threading on the ball and ended up looking more like a golf ball!  <br/>=(  <br/>Anyone know why that is and how to avoid that? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>If you haven''t got an answer to the resizing question yet, check out  <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a> tutorial.</td>', 'Originally posted by esulbi: Actually, that is a softball in a pond under a bridge.  It looked all soaked and pathetic sitting there with the leaves that washed up with it.  For some reason, when I resized the photo, it lost the detail of the threading on the ball and ended up looking more like a golf ball!  =(  Anyone know why that is and how to avoid that?   If you haven''t got an answer to the resizing question yet, check out  this tutorial.', '2005-11-17 09:21:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1876599, 254617, 43809, '<td valign="top">Congrats man...a well deserved ribbon...great effort!!!</td>', 'Congrats man...a well deserved ribbon...great effort!!!', '2005-11-17 09:54:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(1876868, 253314, 43809, '<td valign="top">thanks for all ur support...<br/>hope to do better in future.</td>', 'thanks for all ur support...hope to do better in future.', '2005-11-17 11:34:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1877022, 255286, 16950, '<td valign="top">This was one of my favorites.  I am surprised it didn''t do better.</td>', 'This was one of my favorites.  I am surprised it didn''t do better.', '2005-11-17 12:55:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1877257, 255603, 3214, '<td valign="top">I rated it lower because it looked like the dog was lying on a mover''s blanket and the lack of shadow detail in the exposure, particularly around the dog''s eye.  I rated it higher because the background objects contributed to the concept of garbage lying about out of focus because of the well-chosen depth of field, and I liked the juxtaposition of it with the healthy flowers.  The tones of the blurred foliage adds a painterly touch.  An angle that would have shown the depth of the mattress would have significantly impacted my scoring.</td>', 'I rated it lower because it looked like the dog was lying on a mover''s blanket and the lack of shadow detail in the exposure, particularly around the dog''s eye.  I rated it higher because the background objects contributed to the concept of garbage lying about out of focus because of the well-chosen depth of field, and I liked the juxtaposition of it with the healthy flowers.  The tones of the blurred foliage adds a painterly touch.  An angle that would have shown the depth of the mattress would have significantly impacted my scoring.', '2005-11-17 14:24:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1877634, 255246, 48205, '<td valign="top">Very nice picture. Nice contrasting. It looks like a painting. Very Warholic!!</td>', 'Very nice picture. Nice contrasting. It looks like a painting. Very Warholic!!', '2005-11-17 16:32:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1877668, 255603, 47117, '<td valign="top">Thank you lynn. I know the angle could have been better. I really did very little editing to this photo and didn''t even take it for this challenge.  Just did a contrast touch I think.  I really entered it last minute since it was in the time frame, but thanks for the input.  Now I am going to look up the word "juxtaposition". LOL....<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thank you lynn. I know the angle could have been better. I really did very little editing to this photo and didn''t even take it for this challenge.  Just did a contrast touch I think.  I really entered it last minute since it was in the time frame, but thanks for the input.  Now I am going to look up the word "juxtaposition". LOL.... ', '2005-11-17 16:44:04.000000', NULL, 0),
