(1883942, 254617, 10016, '<td valign="top">Does anyone else see two rusty faces in this photo?  Maybe I''ve been staring at it too long.<br/> <br/>I added some labels to the image to point it out.  The blue arrow points to a second "face" that is a little harder to see.  Tilt your head 45 degrees to the right and you might make it out.  It looks like a little "alien" to me.<br/> <br/>I thought it was cool, but then I''m running on very little sleep :^)<br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.larryejohnson.com/garbage.jpg'', strrpos(''//www.larryejohnson.com/garbage.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.larryejohnson.com/garbage.jpg"/></td>', 'Does anyone else see two rusty faces in this photo?  Maybe I''ve been staring at it too long. I added some labels to the image to point it out.  The blue arrow points to a second "face" that is a little harder to see.  Tilt your head 45 degrees to the right and you might make it out.  It looks like a little "alien" to me. I thought it was cool, but then I''m running on very little sleep :^) ', '2005-11-19 23:26:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1883975, 253346, 24500, '<td valign="top">As a thumbnail I thought I was looking at blueberries.  Then I saw the Garbage challenge followed by your incredible photo subject.  It is so difficult to decide what to accept as unpublished or sanitized images coming from Irak here in Canada.  Nobody want''s to be stuck in what I describe in your photo as the dry mud.  War horror is implied by your damaged "fruits".  I think that color is important due to blue also meaning sad when hardship strikes and a style of song that reveals or heals inner pain.  It is also UN cap identifying ultimate goal of peace.  Great photo.  Thanks for sharing,<br/>by Donald</td>', 'As a thumbnail I thought I was looking at blueberries.  Then I saw the Garbage challenge followed by your incredible photo subject.  It is so difficult to decide what to accept as unpublished or sanitized images coming from Irak here in Canada.  Nobody want''s to be stuck in what I describe in your photo as the dry mud.  War horror is implied by your damaged "fruits".  I think that color is important due to blue also meaning sad when hardship strikes and a style of song that reveals or heals inner pain.  It is also UN cap identifying ultimate goal of peace.  Great photo.  Thanks for sharing,by Donald', '2005-11-19 23:46:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1884328, 253710, 39243, '<td valign="top">Akasha I am not sure if that is a time date on your pic but you were already DQ''ed for another pic with text added if you get 3 you end up being not able to submit for a while - be careful and good luck.<br/></td>', 'Akasha I am not sure if that is a time date on your pic but you were already DQ''ed for another pic with text added if you get 3 you end up being not able to submit for a while - be careful and good luck.', '2005-11-20 03:31:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1884331, 255590, 39243, '<td valign="top">I went to look at your real photography and it is quite nice. I do think it is funny that you aimed for the brown and got it. (you were aiming for the brown weren''t you?)</td>', 'I went to look at your real photography and it is quite nice. I do think it is funny that you aimed for the brown and got it. (you were aiming for the brown weren''t you?)', '2005-11-20 03:35:55.000000', NULL, 0),
